      "writtenOn": "2026-07-21T22:40:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can\u0027t we just properly set `pgd` and `agaw` for `pt_domain` itself in the first place (i.e. in `init_pt_domain()`)? So that we can use `\u0026pt_domain` the same way as \"normal\" domains returned by `pkvm_get_iommu_domain()` (and thus avoid these confusing `domain_ptr` and `cache_domain` variables referring to the same thing, and so on).\n\nIt seems we can even go further and pass both `pgd` and `did` to `pkvm_get_iommu_domain()`, to let `pkvm_get_iommu_domain()` itself return `\u0026pt_domain` instead of a \"normal\" domain if needed (and let `pkvm_put_iommu_domain()` do nothing for `\u0026pt_domain`), and thus avoid all this boilerplate on the caller side (and thus also avoid the need for that `release_entry_domain()` helper for hiding this boilerplate)?\n\nMore precisely, we can, for example, rename the existing `pkvm_get_iommu_domain()` and `pkvm_put_iommu_domain()` (which don\u0027t take `did`) to `__pkvm_get_iommu_domain()` and `__pkvm_put_iommu_domain()` and make them static, to use them only inside `pkvm/domain.c` (in pkvm_iommu_domain_map()/pkvm_iommu_domain_unmap()/pkvm_free_iommu_domain()). And then provide public functions like:\n\n```\nstruct dmar_domain *pkvm_get_iommu_domain(void *pgd, u16 did)\n{\n\tif (did \u003d\u003d FLPT_DEFAULT_DID)\n\t\treturn \u0026pt_domain;\n\t\t\n\treturn __pkvm_get_iommu_domain(pgd);\n}\n\nstruct dmar_domain *pkvm_get_iommu_domain_noref(void *pgd, u16 did)\n{\n\tif (did \u003d\u003d FLPT_DEFAULT_DID)\n\t\treturn \u0026pt_domain;\n\t\t\n\treturn __pkvm_get_iommu_domain_noref(pgd);\n}\n\nvoid pkvm_put_iommu_domain(struct dmar_domain *domain)\n{\n\tif (domain \u003d\u003d \u0026pt_domain)\n\t\treturn;\n\t\t\n\t__pkvm_put_iommu_domain(pgd);\n}\n```\n\n?",
      "revId": "80730d53a934c05f3620e4e1549e683d8bc668af",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
